 "release": 0.25,
 "sustained": false,
 "gain": 1.18,
 "notes": "Five-octave concert marimba, yarn mallets, mezzo-forte, anechoic (dry) mono. 21 notes C2-C7 every minor third, natural decay (about 3-4 s in the bass, about 2 s at the top). The instrument is tuned about 10-24 cents sharp (A442-ish); notes were retuned to A440. Recommended release 0.2-0.3 s (bars ring freely; a longer release sounds more natural than a hard cut)."
